00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:41.700
But the idea that they're floating this on
Twitter could lead to Trump talking about

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.470
it in more detail.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.750
And these are effectively Willie Horton ads.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.420
Willie Horton ads are still studied and discussed
today if you don't know what they are.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:55.100
Back in 1988, Massachusetts Governor Michael
Dukakis, who has been a guest on this program

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:02.090
multiple times, was the Democratic nominee
and was running against George H.W. Bush.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:06.800
And George H.W. Bush started publicizing with
a variety of different so-called Willie Horton

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.599
ads, how Michael Dukakis let Willie Horton
out.

00:02:11.599 --> 00:02:15.999
And it was the start of this idea of Democrats.

00:02:15.999 --> 00:02:20.269
It was more officially codifying the idea
of Democrats are going to release dangerous

00:02:20.269 --> 00:02:22.299
black people into society.

00:02:22.299 --> 00:02:23.760
You aren't safe.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.670
Vote for the Republican who will actually
keep you safe.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.640
This is the exact same thing that we are seeing
from the Trump campaign.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.469
And when you step back and, you know, they're
tweeting mug shots of black people, I mean,

00:02:34.469 --> 00:02:38.010
it's just it's fully brazen at this point
in time.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.810
Trump's continued use of the term China virus,
he's talked about, you know, Cung, flu wuv,

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:49.889
horn flu, all of this stuff back at the beginning
of his campaign.

00:02:49.889 --> 00:02:52.060
Mexico is not sending its best.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.749
